1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
Today, we're going to discuss pH electrode maintenance.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:08,740
You want to maintain your electrode to keep them fast, accurate, and functioning as well

3
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:13,820
as to keep them clean for contamination and make sure that they are working properly.

4
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:18,500
The first steps every day when you go into the lab is you want to start by removing

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,580
your electrode from the storage solution bottle.

6
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:27,620
To remove the electrode, first unscrew the cap of the bottle and slowly remove the

7
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:35,940
electrode as to not create a vacuum. Once the electrode is removed, you want to make

8
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:39,120
sure that you fill it up all the way before using it.

9
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:44,220
Locate the fill hole on the side and using the appropriate fill solution, fill the

10
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:48,500
electrode all the way to the fill hole. You always want to make sure that your

11
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:52,240
internal fill solution is at least one inch above your sample at which you are

12
00:00:52,240 --> 00:01:01,100
measuring. Once your electrode is filled, you can begin to start measuring your

13
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:05,420
samples. In order to keep your electrode clean, you want to make sure that you

14
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:09,580
change your storage solution at least twice a month. To do this, dump out your

15
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,380
original storage solution and rinse out the storage bottle some deionized water.

16
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:19,940
Make sure you rinse it out multiple times and swirl it around to remove any old

17
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:30,870
storage solution. Then you want to choose the appropriate storage solution for

18
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:36,110
your electrode and fill the storage bottle at least 60% of the way. You want

19
00:01:36,110 --> 00:01:39,710
to make sure that the entire bulb of your electrode is sitting in storage

20
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:48,610
solution to keep that bulb clean and functioning properly. To place your

21
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:53,170
electrode back in the storage solution bottle, loosely fit the cap and slide the

22
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:57,370
electrode in. You want to make sure to tighten the cap once the electrode is

23
00:01:57,370 --> 00:02:06,840
fully in and cover the fill hole for overnight storage. The next segment of

24
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:11,120
this video, we will show you how to drain and refill a short flow electrode.

25
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:16,160
Using a silver, silver chloride electrode, we're going to drain and refill the

26
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:21,560
internal fill solution. First, you want to start by taking that electrode out of

27
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:25,600
the storage bottle, again making sure that you don't create a vacuum while

28
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:32,180
removing the electrode. Once the electrode is removed from the storage bottle,

29
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:38,580
using a waste beaker, you're going to uncap the fill hole and then press

30
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:42,260
down on the top of the electrode until all of the internal fill solution has

31
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:49,630
drained. Using the appropriate filling solution, you're then going to fill the

32
00:02:49,630 --> 00:02:54,590
electrode by locating the fill hole on the side of the electrode and filling it

33
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:59,590
all the way to the top. Since this is a short flow electrode, there is always a

34
00:02:59,590 --> 00:03:03,550
small amount of solution moving through the electrode. You want to make sure that

35
00:03:03,550 --> 00:03:09,930
you top this off every day before using it. Once the electrode is filled,

36
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:15,050
you may then rinse off your electrode if there's any excess fill solution

37
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:19,890
with some deionized water. Now your electrode is clean and ready for use.

38
00:03:19,890 --> 00:03:32,270
Either put it back into storage or you may start using it on your samples.

39
00:03:32,270 --> 00:03:37,850
The next segment of this video, we're going to show you how to refill a non-sher

40
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:42,550
flow electrode by first draining it and then filling it. We are going to

41
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:46,990
demonstrate how to remove the fill solution from a non-sher flow electrode

42
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:52,990
by using a glass bodied Ross electrode. First remove the electrode from the

43
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:56,910
storage bottle, then you're going to locate the fill hole on the side of the

44
00:03:56,910 --> 00:04:02,070
electrode. Using a waste beaker and a disposable pipette, we're going to

45
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:07,190
remove the inner fill solution. Gently stick the tip of the pipette into the

46
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:11,070
electrode fill hole and invert the electrode so you can easily access the

47
00:04:11,070 --> 00:04:15,630
fill solution. Then using the pipette, you're going to remove the fill

48
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:20,790
solution until there's none left. When you get to the end it may be hard to get

49
00:04:20,790 --> 00:04:24,310
the rest of the fill solution out so you can shake the electrode to try to get

50
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:29,670
out the last remaining drops. Then using the appropriate fill solution, we're

51
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:34,670
going to top off the electrode. Insert the tip of the filling bottle into the

52
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:45,160
fill hole and fill the electrode all the way up. Since this is a refillable

53
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:49,640
electrode, you want to make sure every day before using it that your inner

54
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:53,120
chamber is filled with inner fill solution so you have the best results

55
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:59,440
while using your electrode. Once it's filled you may start either sampling or

56
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:02,640
put it back into storage.
